A||N||7||Tom Philips||Front suspension tight||||5||
Z||000000||Tom Philips||12-13-2000||08:51 AM||||Hello all my first post and i have a question ? I replaced all the front end bushings with poly and after putting vehicle back together the front end will not deflect (pushing down on front fenders) was wondering if this is common on bushing replacement and using poly?<BR>86 SE<BR>88 Gt<BR><P>------------------<BR>||||reg||5
Z||000001||Oreif||12-13-2000||10:14 AM||||Did you properly grease the poly bushings? It should be a little stiffer but you should still be able to push down on the suspension. It's not far off of stock.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Tom Philips||12-13-2000||10:39 AM||||Yes i did grease bushings and actually installed grease fittings in case there were any squeaks in the future.. Just seems real tight... <P>------------------<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000003||DougV||12-13-2000||10:55 AM||||Did you do the FINAL tourque of all suspension parts while the wheels were on the ground??? Otherwise the bushings are preloaded.||||reg||1
Z||000004||Tom Philips||12-13-2000||11:39 AM||||The sleeve inside the bushing will rotate 360 degrees and i did not think it mattered if torque was applied with wheels on or off the ground.... but maybee i am wrong||||reg||1
Z||000005||ThatRickGuy||12-13-2000||12:31 PM||||Okay, maybe I did this a little different, but when I replaced my upper bushing, I never took the weight off the lower joint. I lifted the car up, took off the tire, stuck a jack stand under the lower a-arm (out by the spindle) and dropped the car down. So then the weight was on all 4 corners as it would be with the tire on. popped the top a-arm off, replaced the bushing (lubed the heck outta 'em) and torque it all back together. Not a squeek scince, altho my lower ball joints need replacing  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"><BR>||||reg||1
Z||000006||bHooper||12-13-2000||01:44 PM||||i'm glad somebody mentioned that today.  i am putting the finishing touches on my Gt tonight, and had planned on taking it to the shop afterwards.<P>man, is it gonna be tight, getting in there with the torque wrench... with the Eibachs and KYB's.<P>hoop||||reg||1
Z||000007||theogre||12-13-2000||07:25 PM||||Poly bushings don't preload. That is a problem unique to OE rubber torsion bushings.||||reg||1
